@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge README · Lark Agent Bridge：<sub>npm package: `@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge` · git repo: `lark-agent-bridge`</sub>

> A Feishu / Lark bridge for local coding agents — *one group, one conversation, one pinned runtime*. Bridges **dsh** (in-process plugin), **CLI** agents (`traex` / `codex`, spawned by a daemon), an **IDE** window (attached over a socket), or a **custom** agent — behind one gateway.

[中文 README](./README.zh.md)

@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge README · Windows PowerShell：The script preflights Node, installs the `lark-workspace` / `lark-readonly`
presets, and registers both the bridge bundle and its `dsh-tool-lark-cli`
dependency. When `dsh` is available it uses the official `dsh plugin` command,bash

@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge README · then, from your dsh checkout:：> ⚠️ A `link:` install points the profile dependency at THIS directory. If you
> later move or delete it, the next `dsh web` cannot resolve the bundle and
> fails to boot. Keep the clone in place, or use Option 1.

@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge README · Option 4: manual install from source (contributors / offline fallback)：Use this only when neither the npm setup script nor the official `dsh plugin`
command fits. It installs from source alongside your dsh checkout.

```bash

@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge README · "bundles": ["@deepseek-ai/dsh-base", "@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-app", "@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge"]：```

Launch dsh (the bundle loads the plugin automatically):

```bash

@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge README · from your dsh checkout：DSH_PERMISSION_MODE=danger-full-access dsh web
```

> `DSH_PERMISSION_MODE=danger-full-access` makes the agent's approval policy `never`. This is needed because Feishu users cannot click through a local approval prompt. Only use it in an environment you trust.

@bihangchi9/lark-agent-bridge README · Access control (security model)：The bot's **security boundary is exactly "who may send it a message"**: every
message becomes an agent turn with host-level permissions, so access is
